            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0129" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/817c: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ireland</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-03">June 3, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. As S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt</hi> appears to have
                    sailed with considerable number of emergency accommodations untaken although
                    those accommodations (approximately 500) were offered at rate of $150, please
                    telegraph reasons and how many were taken and how many untaken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
